# Trivy allowlist — every entry below MUST carry a justification comment.
# Applies to both the CI config/fs scans (ci.yml) and the CD image scan
# (cd.yml). Renovate keeps base images and dependencies patched, so entries
# here should be re-reviewed whenever the underlying CVE/finding is fixed
# upstream and removed once it no longer applies.

# --- infra/k8s config scan --------------------------------------------------
# KSV-0014 / KSV-0118: infra-dev/postgres/deployment.yaml runs without a
# read-only root filesystem / explicit securityContext. infra-dev/ is the
# LOCAL DEV convenience Postgres only (never applied to prod — the prod
# overlay points every service at an external managed database instead, see
# infra/k8s/overlays/prod/kustomization.yaml). Owned by the k8s-manifests
# phase; hardening it is tracked there, not blocking this CI/CD slice.
KSV-0014
KSV-0118

# KSV-0046: observability/prometheus-adapter/rbac.yaml grants the
# custom-metrics ClusterRole read access to all API groups/resources. This
# is the upstream k8s-prometheus-adapter requirement for discovering custom
# metrics cluster-wide to serve the HPA custom-metrics API (8c-B) — scoping
# it down breaks metric discovery. Read-only (get/list/watch), not a write
# grant. Owned by the k8s-manifests phase.
KSV-0046

# --- filesystem vulnerability scan (pnpm-lock.yaml) -------------------------
# Both are transitive devDependencies pulled in deep under @nx/webpack and
# @nx/jest (build/test tooling only) — never reach the runtime image, which
# npm-installs only the webpack-bundled app's pruned package.json + pg (see
# infra/docker/Dockerfile). Fixed versions live several major bumps up the
# @nx/* toolchain; Renovate will surface the bump once upstream releases it.
# CVE-2026-14257: brace-expansion ReDoS, via minimatch -> fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin -> @nx/webpack.
CVE-2026-14257
# GHSA-pm4m-ph32-ghv5: js-yaml ReDoS, via babel-plugin-istanbul -> @jest/transform -> @nx/jest.
GHSA-pm4m-ph32-ghv5
